# camelCase Naming

Classes, functions, and IDs must use **camelCase**.

```js
// ❌ BAD
function render_mini_map() {}
const KeyBoard_Controls = () => {};
document.querySelector('#mini-map');

// ✅ GOOD
function renderMiniMap() {}
const keyBoardControls = () => {};
document.querySelector('#miniMap');
```

```scss
// ❌ BAD
.mini-map { }
#key-board-controls { }

// ✅ GOOD
.miniMap { }
#keyBoardControls { }
```

Do not use kebab-case, snake_case, or PascalCase for class names or IDs. React component identifiers may remain PascalCase; CSS class/id strings and non-component functions should be camelCase.
